description:
Design a custom NAND gate chip that processes a 9-bit input. It produces a 2-bit output where the first bit is the result of a NAND operation on the least significant bits in[0] and in[1], and the second bit is the result of a NAND operation on the next four bits in[2], in[3], in[4], and in[5]. The module is implemented using both continuous assignments and procedural blocks to ensure the correct output is generated based on the input signals.
module top_module(
  input [8:0] in,
  output reg [1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [8:0] in,
  output reg [1:0] out
);always @(in) begin
    out[0] <= ~(in[0] & in[1]);
    out[1] <= ~(in[2] & in[3] & in[4] & in[5]);
  end

endmodule

