description:
Design a sequential circuit that monitors two input signals, r_a and r_b, on the rising edge of a clock signal (clk) to produce two output signals, r_d and r_e. The output r_e will be set to HIGH when both inputs are HIGH and set to LOW when both inputs are LOW. The output r_d will be set to LOW when r_a is HIGH and r_b is LOW, and set to HIGH when r_a is LOW and r_b is HIGH. This module effectively functions as a conditional output control based on the states of the two input signals.
module top_module(clk,r_a,r_b,r_d,r_e
    );

code:
module top_module(clk,r_a,r_b,r_d,r_e
    );input clk;
         input r_a;
         input r_b;
         output reg r_d,r_e;
always @(posedge clk) begin
        if(r_a==1 && r_b==1) begin
        r_e<=1;
        end
        if(r_a==0 && r_b==0) begin
        r_e<=0;
        end
        if(r_a==1 && r_b==0) begin
        r_d<=0;
        end
        if(r_a==0 && r_b==1) begin
        r_d<=1;
        end
end
endmodule

