description:
Design a Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) circuit. The module takes a clock input and an n-bit control signal to adjust the duty cycle of the PWM signal output. The counter increments on each clock cycle and compares its value to a threshold determined by the control signal. When the counter reaches or exceeds the threshold, the output is set high; otherwise, it is set low. This allows for varying the width of the PWM pulse based on the control signal, making it suitable for applications such as motor control or signal generation.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [n-1:0] ctrl,
  output reg pwm_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [n-1:0] ctrl,
  output reg pwm_out
);parameter n = 8; // number of bits used to represent the control signal

reg [n-1:0] counter;
reg [n:0] threshold;

always @ (posedge clk) begin
  counter <= counter + 1;
  if (counter >= threshold) begin
    pwm_out <= 1;
  end else begin
    pwm_out <= 0;
  end
end

always @ (ctrl) begin
  threshold <= ctrl;
end

endmodule

