description:
Design a finite state machine (FSM) that converts a 4-bit binary input into its corresponding 4-bit Gray code representation. The FSM operates on the rising edge of the clock signal, where it transitions between states based on the input binary value and outputs the appropriate Gray code after processing. The state machine essentially utilizes a series of XOR operations applied to the binary input to generate the Gray code outputs, ensuring that adjacent values differ by only one bit, thereby facilitating error reduction in digital communications and data conversion applications.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [3:0] binary,
  output reg [3:0] gray
);

