description:
Design a register with a specified bit width that updates its stored value on the rising edge of the clock. When enabled by the `en_write` signal, it loads the input data, `data_in`, into the output `data_out`. If the `reset` signal is asserted, the output is set to a predetermined `RESET_VALUE`, which defaults to zero. This module serves as a basic storage element in digital circuits, commonly used in sequential logic designs.
module top_module(
input clk, reset, en_write,
input[BIT_WIDTH - 1: 0] data_in,
output reg signed [BIT_WIDTH - 1: 0] data_out
);

code:
module top_module(
input clk, reset, en_write,
input[BIT_WIDTH - 1: 0] data_in,
output reg signed [BIT_WIDTH - 1: 0] data_out
);parameter BIT_WIDTH = 32;
parameter RESET_VALUE = 0;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (reset == 1'b1)
        data_out <= RESET_VALUE;
    else if (en_write == 1'b1)
        data_out <= data_in;
end

endmodule

